---
import ArticleLayout from "@layouts/ArticleLayout.astro";
import SlateArt from "@components/art/slate.astro";
---

<ArticleLayout
  title="Slate"
  description="A Pencil-first journal for iPad. Exploring the feel of digital ink, a custom brush engine and the simple rhythm of one page per day."
  subtitle="A quieter place to think with your hands."
  eyebrow="2026 · Building / Flowforest"
>
  <SlateArt slot="art" />

  <section>
    <h2>One page, one day</h2>
    <p>
      Slate is a Pencil-first daily journal and planner for iPad. A dated page
      gives the experience a simple structure, leaving the surface itself open
      for thinking, sketching and planning.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>The feel is part of the product</h2>
    <p>
      The project explores a custom Metal brush engine rather than PencilKit.
      Touch sampling, smoothing and ink rendering sit alongside paper patterns
      and a brush studio. This is where interaction design meets the details of
      implementation.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Still on the drawing board</h2>
    <p>
      The repository includes storage, PDF export and sync implementations.
      Native device validation and the feel of the complete experience remain
      part of the ongoing work. The illustration above is an interface study,
      not a capture from a finished app.
    </p>
  </section>
  <aside class="project-status">
    In development · The visual is a portfolio interface study. Features
    described reflect project documentation, rather than a released product.
  </aside>
  <a class="text-link" href="/journal/runway/">
    Next build note ↗
  </a>
</ArticleLayout>
